From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandru Gagniuc <mr.nuke.me@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Jan 2026 22:33:42 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_wcss: add native IPQ9574 support

Backport the public native IPQ9574 clock/reset startup and powerdown
sequences, including the optional auxiliary startup stage. Remove the
unused clock fields and use the documented Q6 reset interface.

Keep startup owned by ath11k, balance preparation and clocks on failures,
and check reset assertions. If cleanup cannot establish a stopped state,
retain the required resources and refuse another load until reboot.
Preserve the reset delay on existing variants and the IPQ9574 polling
budget. This does not establish successful runtime recovery.

Fold the dependent adaptations into this patch so the final implementation
is reviewed directly, without introducing and replacing intermediate code.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260109043352.3072933-2-mr.nuke.me@gmail.com
